  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 109 AM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures around the area are in the upper 50s to \nlow 60s as much colder air has moved in behind a cold front. Winds \nare out of the north and generally less than 15 mph. Drier weather \ntoday and Friday as high pressure becomes dominant through the end \nof the work week.\n\nThe precipitation chances for Saturday have pretty much disappeared. \nThe low has moved north, but also there isn't much moisture at all. \nTemperatures today, Friday, and Sunday are expected to be cooler, \nhighs in the upper 50s to mid 60s. Saturday and the beginning of \nnext week will be 5 to 10 degrees above average. Winds Friday on the \nbackside of the high will gust 30 to near 40 mph west of the \nMissouri River, and 30-35 mph between the Missouri River and US 281. \nThese stronger winds are expected to continue into the evening. \nWinds will increase around the Prairie Coteau through the morning \nhours. Winds Monday will once again gust 30-35 mph across central \nSD, spreading east to the James River.",
